content:
i think HT/Aessinas has a clear use atm as a tool for tank healing within a normal Regrowth/NG build, but a pure HT/Moonglow doesn't really make sense atm simply because Regrowth is so good and improved Regrowth is so easy to pick up, even for a playstyle like mine this run (where I barely ever cast Regrowth) I still might as well have picked up Regrowth due to there being so few other good talents.
for my run earlier tonight i used this build: https://talents.turtle-wow.org/druid?points=oACYYKFYBIAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAFApADIDEIQAAAAA=
where I swap Improved Regrowth for Moonkin Form and Vengeance. It's a bit of a meme but I think it could be an interesting way to try and *balance* a pure HT build moving forward, tying it together with a Wrath spamming Moonkin build
